To create a Discord bot with the `ban` command using Discord.js v14, follow these steps:

1. Create a new Discord application on the [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications) and add a new bot to it.

2. Generate a token for your bot and keep it safe.

3. Install Discord.js v14 using npm by running the following command in your terminal:

   ```
   npm install discord.js
   ```

4. Create a new file named `index.js` in your project directory.

5. Add the following code to your `index.js` file:

```javascript
const { Client, GatewayIntentBits } = require('discord.js');

// Replace with your bot token
const token = 'YOUR_BOT_TOKEN_HERE';

const client = new Client({
  intents: [
    GatewayIntentBits.Guilds,
    GatewayIntentBits.GuildMessages,
    GatewayIntentBits.MessageContent,
  ],
});

client.on('ready', () => {
  console.log(`Logged in as ${client.user.tag}`);
});

client.on('interactionCreate', async interaction => {
  if (!interaction.isCommand()) return;

  const { commandName, options } = interaction;

  if (commandName === 'ban') {
    const userId = options.getMember('user').id;

    // Perform the ban operation
    await interaction.guild.members.ban(userId, { days: 7, reason: 'Banned by bot' });

    await interaction.reply({
      content: `User ${options.getMember('user').user.tag} has been banned.`,
      ephemeral: true,
    });
  }
});

client.login(token);
```

6. Save the file and run the following command in your terminal:

   ```
   node index.js
   ```

7. In your Discord server, go to the "Applications" section in your Discord Developer Portal and select your application.

8. Click on the "Bot" tab and scroll down to the "Scopes" section.

9. Enable the following scopes:

   - `bot:ApplicationCommands`
   - `bot:MessageContent`

10. In your Discord server, enable the bot by clicking the "Add to Server" button and following the prompts.

11. In your Discord server, type `/ban @user` to test the command. Replace `@user` with the username or ID of the user you want to ban.

That's it! Your Discord bot now has a `ban` command using Discord.js v14. Note that the `ban` command requires the `Manage Messages` permission in the server to work. Make sure your bot has this permission before using the command.

Here's an example implementation of a C++ function that converts Markdown to HTML using the popular Markdown library, **pandoc**:

